Vera Rubin — the first multi-rack, pod-scale

00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:49.840
supercomputer built for the agentic age.
It starts at TSMC. The seven new chips

00:42:49.840 --> 00:42:54.240
that make up Vera Rubin take shape 
through hundreds of processing steps.

00:42:54.240 --> 00:43:03.280
Three-nanometer process. CoWoS advanced packaging. 
HBM4 memory from Micron, SK Hynix, and Samsung.

00:43:03.280 --> 00:43:10.880
The Vera Rubin GPU — six trillion transistors 
with over 18,000 components on one board.

00:43:10.880 --> 00:43:18.000
Vera Rubin NVL72 does the thinking — prompt and 
context understanding, reasoning, and planning.

00:43:18.000 --> 00:43:26.560
Next, a new modular compute tray — streamlined 
with a new PCB midplane. ConnectX-9,

00:43:26.560 --> 00:43:32.160
SuperNICs, and BlueField-4 DPUs — all 
