01:00:08.222 --> 01:00:10.000
[VIDEO NARRATION]
Agentic AI changes the role

01:00:10.000 --> 01:00:17.840
of the CPU. The CPU is now the conductor, and 
the GPU is the orchestra. Traditional CPUs were

01:00:17.840 --> 01:00:24.480
built for a different era — maximizing cores per 
socket, slicing them up, virtualizing, renting by

01:00:24.480 --> 01:00:32.480
the hour. In the age of agents, the CPU is now a 
bottleneck to GPU utilization, directly affecting

01:00:32.480 --> 01:00:39.920
token throughput, latency, and user experience.
NVIDIA Vera is the CPU built for the agentic

01:00:39.920 --> 01:00:45.680
loop — combining NVIDIA’s custom data center 
CPU core with a scalable coherency fabric,

01:00:45.680 --> 01:00:51.120
for the right balance of performance, cores, 
and bandwidth to maximize AI factory health.

01:00:51.120 --> 01:00:55.920
At the heart of Vera is the NVIDIA 
Olympus core, built for modern data

01:00:55.920 --> 01:01:03.520
center workloads — branch-heavy Python runtimes, 
tool calls, and sandbox code execution. Each core

01:01:03.520 --> 01:01:10.320
is tuned for throughput. A neural branch predictor 
evaluating two taken branches per cycle. A 10-wide

01:01:10.320 --> 01:01:15.920
decode engine brings in more work each cycle. 
A large out-of-order engine keeps instructions

01:01:15.920 --> 01:01:21.760
moving. Advanced prefetchers with a novel 
graph engine anticipating the next data fetch.

01:01:21.760 --> 01:01:27.920
But fast cores only matter when data 
arrives correctly and on time. Vera is

01:01:27.920 --> 01:01:34.560
the first CPU to use LPDDR5X memory while 
correcting multiple errors simultaneously

01:01:34.560 --> 01:01:39.920
without compromising bandwidth. Vera 
achieves 40% lower peak memory latency

01:01:39.920 --> 01:01:47.440
versus x86, keeping cores fed on time through 
retrieval, analytics, and sandbox execution.

01:01:47.440 --> 01:01:53.840
NVIDIA’s second-generation scalable coherence 
fabric unifies all 88 Olympus cores on a

01:01:53.840 --> 01:02:02.480
monolithic mesh. Separate dies for memory and 
cores are not split across chiplets, enabling 50%

01:02:02.480 --> 01:02:09.280
faster core-to-core communication than traditional 
CPUs. And memory-coherent NVLink chip-to-chip

01:02:09.280 --> 01:02:17.360
connects GPUs directly to the CPU. Beyond GPUs, 
NVLink chip-to-chip can scale Vera up to multiple

01:02:17.360 --> 01:02:25.200
sockets, enabling massive bandwidth between CPUs.
Vera delivers 1.8 times the agentic sandbox

01:02:25.200 --> 01:02:32.480
performance of x86 CPUs. Standalone, Vera 
racks run agent sandboxes, tools, code,

01:02:32.480 --> 01:02:39.600
and data pipelines. Tightly coupled to Rubin 
GPUs, Vera keeps accelerated workloads moving.

01:02:39.600 --> 01:02:49.840
NVIDIA Vera BlueField-4 STX — powers context, 
memory, and AI storage. Compute, network, storage.

01:02:49.840 --> 01:03:01.031
Vera is the CPU for the age of agents.
