[VIDEO NARRATION]

01:12:46.400 --> 01:12:53.280
Cadence and NVIDIA are partnering to build chip 
design agents. Hundreds of thousands of NVIDIA

01:12:53.280 --> 01:12:59.200
chips come together to make the AI factories 
that power the world’s frontier AI models.

01:12:59.200 --> 01:13:05.200
Designing these chips, and the systems they run 
in, is one of the hardest engineering challenges.

01:13:05.200 --> 01:13:11.680
Trillions of transistors. Three-dimensional 
circuits at microscopic scale. Every gate,

01:13:11.680 --> 01:13:18.640
every wire, synchronized to picoseconds, must work 
in perfect harmony, with no margin for error.

01:13:18.640 --> 01:13:24.880
Physical prototypes are too slow and too costly. 
So engineers work in the digital realm. Each chip

01:13:24.880 --> 01:13:30.800
begins as a set of architectural specifications, 
then translated into RTL — the language of chip

01:13:30.800 --> 01:13:38.560
design. RTL must be verified in simulation. A 
single bug can delay a chip by months. At NVIDIA,

01:13:38.560 --> 01:13:44.400
thousands of engineers, billions of compute 
hours per year, millions of tests written, run,

01:13:44.400 --> 01:13:50.640
and debugged — a cycle that takes teams weeks.
To compress this cycle, Cadence and NVIDIA built

01:13:50.640 --> 01:13:57.200
a design verification agent. Codex orchestrates 
the process. Cadence Chip Stack launches the

01:13:57.200 --> 01:14:03.920
RTL verification loop, powered by Nemotron 
and secured by NVIDIA OpenShell. Calling on

01:14:03.920 --> 01:14:11.280
expert subagents in RTL generation, test bench 
creation, regression testing, and debug. The

01:14:11.280 --> 01:14:17.040
system drives itself. The Chip Stack agents run 
hundreds of simulations with Cadence Xcelium,

01:14:17.040 --> 01:14:24.720
formal verification with JasperGold. Design flaws 
revealed. Bugs in the code, fixed. What once took

01:14:24.720 --> 01:14:32.800
weeks now takes hours. Verification cycles over 
40 times faster. Together, NVIDIA and Cadence are

01:14:32.800 --> 01:14:38.880
reinventing chip design with AI agents.
