01:38:42.560 --> 01:38:52.000
However, in order to create data for AI robotics, 
it has to be from the perspective of the robot.

01:38:52.000 --> 01:38:58.480
And most of the world’s video data is from 
a third person, not first person. And so,

01:38:58.480 --> 01:39:06.000
agentic systems, robotic systems, physical 
AI — the data is the hardest problem.

01:39:06.000 --> 01:39:11.680
You’ve seen us move up this ladder. We started 
with teleoperation, which is basically human

01:39:11.680 --> 01:39:17.120
demonstration — no different than the big 
breakthrough of reinforcement learning from human

01:39:17.120 --> 01:39:23.600
feedback. Then we use simulation — this is 
where Omniverse comes in, no different than

01:39:23.600 --> 01:39:34.080
reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards. 
We use these systems to bootstrap the AI model,

01:39:34.080 --> 01:39:41.680
the physical AI model. Eventually we’re able 
to learn from third-person data, reprojecting

01:39:41.680 --> 01:39:48.960
into first person. And now, eventually, through 
bootstrapping, we have a World Foundation Model

01:39:48.960 --> 01:39:55.840
that can understand the physical world from any 
perspective you want — third person, first person,

01:39:56.480 --> 01:40:07.520
inside and out. This is a big breakthrough.
