01:41:01.902 --> 01:41:03.440
[VIDEO NARRATION]
The real world is infinite

01:41:03.440 --> 01:41:10.880
and unpredictable. Physical AI needs data, 
but real-world data is impossible to scale.

01:41:10.880 --> 01:41:20.000
For physical AI, compute is data. This is Cosmos 
— an open frontier omni-model for physical AI,

01:41:20.000 --> 01:41:25.120
built on a new Mixture of Transformers 
architecture. Pixels, action, sound,

01:41:25.120 --> 01:41:28.240
and language flow into the 
autoregressive transformer,

01:41:28.240 --> 01:41:35.200
which reasons, plans, and instructs the diffusion 
transformer, which generates what comes next.

01:41:35.200 --> 01:41:41.040
Developers post-train Cosmos across 
embodiments and use cases. As a VLM,

01:41:41.040 --> 01:41:48.240
Cosmos watches the physical world, understands 
what’s happening, describing scenes and flagging

01:41:48.240 --> 01:41:56.080
what matters. As a world model, Cosmos generates 
physics-accurate synthetic video from an image,

01:41:56.080 --> 01:42:03.920
text, or video. As a simulator, Cosmos closes 
the loop for policy training and evaluation.

01:42:03.920 --> 01:42:09.840
And as the foundation of NVIDIA OmniDreams 
— an action-conditioned world model — Cosmos

01:42:09.840 --> 01:42:16.080
predicts the future frame by frame.
Post-train Cosmos and it becomes a world

01:42:16.080 --> 01:42:26.640
action model — perceiving, reasoning, planning, 
generating actions — for robots of every kind,

01:42:26.640 --> 01:42:33.840
for everything that moves. A new 
kind of data. A new kind of teacher,

01:42:33.840 --> 01:42:55.360
generated by compute. Cosmos — the foundation 
for developers in the age of physical AI.

01:42:55.360 --> 01:42:55.920
